  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$George Miller and the Limits of Working Memory$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$George Miller and the Limits of Working Memory$q$, $q$In 1956, the psychologist George Miller published a paper with an unusually playful title: 'The Magical Number Seven, Plus or Minus Two'. In it, he reviewed a range of experiments on how much information people can hold in mind at one time. Whether the task involved remembering digits, letters, or words, performance seemed to break down at roughly the same point. Most adults, Miller observed, could keep about seven items in immediate memory, give or take two.

Miller was careful to note that the number was less important than the unit being counted. People could remember about seven random letters, but they could also remember about seven words, each of which contained several letters. The mind, he argued, does not store raw information but organizes it into meaningful groups, which he called chunks. A telephone number, for instance, is far easier to recall as three groups than as a string of ten separate digits.

This process of chunking explains how experts can seem to have extraordinary memories. A chess master looking at a board does not see thirty-two individual pieces but a handful of familiar patterns. In one famous demonstration, a student trained himself to recall over eighty digits by connecting them to running times he knew well. His memory for random letters, however, remained ordinary, since his chunking strategy did not apply to them.

Later research has revised Miller's figure downward, with many psychologists now suggesting that the true limit is closer to four chunks. Yet the central insight remains: working memory is small, and its effective size depends on how well information is organized. Miller went on to help found the field of cognitive science, and his paper is still among the most cited in psychology.$q$, $q$psychology$q$, 5, 287, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_B$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$An appropriate title for this text would be —$q$, $q$["The Career of George Miller", "How Chess Masters Remember Positions", "The Limits of Working Memory and the Power of Chunking", "Why Seven Is a Magical Number"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. הקריירה של מילר מוזכרת רק במשפט האחרון.", "לא נכון. שחקני השחמט הם דוגמה אחת מהפסקה השלישית.", "נכון. הכותרת מקיפה את שני הרעיונות המרכזיים — גבול הזיכרון והדרך שבה קיבוץ מידע מרחיב אותו.", "לא נכון. הקטע דווקא מציין שהמספר עצמו פחות חשוב, ושמחקר מאוחר תיקן אותו כלפי מטה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$main_idea$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch B, passage=miller-seven, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the third paragraph, why did the student's memory for letters remain ordinary?$q$, $q$["Because he had practiced only with digits for a few weeks.", "Because letters are naturally harder to remember than numbers.", "Because he had no interest in learning to recall letters.", "Because his grouping method did not suit letters."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה אינה מציינת את משך האימון.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אינה טוענת שאותיות קשות יותר לזכירה מטבען.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אינה מזכירה את רצונו או עניינו של הסטודנט.", "נכון. הפסקה מסבירה שאסטרטגיית הקיבוץ שלו, שהתבססה על זמני ריצה, לא התאימה לאותיות."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, $q$["since his chunking strategy did not apply to them"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch B, passage=miller-seven, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the last paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["explain how telephone numbers are chunked.", "note later revisions to Miller's figure while affirming his core insight.", "describe Miller's role in founding cognitive science.", "argue that Miller's estimate of seven items was correct and later researchers were wrong."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. דוגמת מספר הטלפון מופיעה בפסקה השנייה.", "נכון. הפסקה מציינת שהמספר תוקן לארבעה, אך מדגישה שהתובנה המרכזית על גודל הזיכרון וארגון המידע נותרה בעינה.", "לא נכון. תפקידו בייסוד מדע הקוגניציה מוזכר במשפט אחד בלבד ואינו מטרת הפסקה.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מקבלת את התיקון כלפי מטה ואינה טוענת שהחוקרים המאוחרים טעו."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch B, passage=miller-seven, q3$q$, 3, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$It can be inferred from the statement that "the number was less important than the unit being counted" that —$q$, $q$["the amount of information a person can hold depends on how that information is grouped.", "Miller believed his figure of seven was inaccurate.", "letters are easier to remember than words.", "counting is the most reliable way to test memory."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. אם היחידה הנספרת חשובה יותר מהמספר, הרי שכמות המידע שאפשר להחזיק תלויה באופן שבו הוא מקובץ — כפי שדוגמת המילים והאותיות מראה.", "לא נכון. מילר לא טען שהמספר שגוי, אלא שהוא פחות חשוב מהיחידה.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מראה שאפשר לזכור כשבע אותיות וגם כשבע מילים, ולא שאותיות קלות יותר.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו עוסק בשיטות לבדיקת זיכרון."]$q$::jsonb, $q$inference$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["the number was less important than the unit being counted"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch B, passage=miller-seven, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$In the first paragraph, the word "playful" is closest in meaning to —$q$, $q$["Scientific", "Confusing to most readers", "Lengthy", "Light-hearted and witty"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. הכותרת מתוארת כיוצאת דופן דווקא משום שאינה נשמעת מדעית ורצינית.", "לא נכון. אין בהקשר רמז לכך שהכותרת מבלבלת.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה עוסקת באורך הכותרת.", "נכון. 'playful' פירושו שובב, קליל ומשועשע — כותרת עם 'מספר קסום' היא יוצאת דופן במאמר מדעי."]$q$::jsonb, $q$vocab_in_context$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["an unusually playful title"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch B, passage=miller-seven, q5$q$, 5, true);
