  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$When the Sahara Was Green$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$When the Sahara Was Green$q$, $q$The Sahara is today the largest hot desert on Earth, yet for thousands of years it was a landscape of grasslands, rivers, and lakes. Geologists refer to this era as the African Humid Period, which lasted roughly from 11,000 to 5,000 years ago. During that time, monsoon rains reached far north of their present limits, and a vast lake, sometimes called Mega-Chad, spread across what is now central Africa.

The explanation lies not on Earth but in its orbit. The planet's axis slowly wobbles over a cycle of about 20,000 years, altering how much sunlight the Northern Hemisphere receives in summer. When summer radiation was stronger, the land heated more intensely, drawing moist air inland from the Atlantic and strengthening the monsoon. Vegetation then reinforced the effect, since plants retain moisture and darken the surface, which absorbs more heat and encourages further rainfall.

The evidence for this greener world is abundant and often striking. Rock paintings in the mountains of Algeria and Libya depict cattle, giraffes, and hippopotamuses, animals that could not survive there today. One famous cave in the Egyptian desert contains images of human figures that appear to be swimming. Sediment cores from the Atlantic record the dust blown off the continent, and they show a sharp decline in dust during the humid period.

How the humid period ended remains a matter of dispute. Some researchers argue that the change was abrupt, with the monsoon collapsing within a few centuries once orbital forcing weakened past a critical threshold. Others contend that the drying was gradual and varied from one region to another. Whatever the pace, the consequences were profound: pastoral communities abandoned the interior, and many appear to have migrated toward the Nile valley. Their arrival there, some scholars suggest, contributed to the concentration of population that preceded the rise of ancient Egypt.$q$, $q$geography / earth science$q$, 6, 302, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_D$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$What is the main idea of the passage?$q$, $q$["Rock paintings in Algeria and Libya prove that giraffes once lived in the Sahara.", "A wobble in Earth's axis controls the strength of the African monsoon.", "The Sahara was once green because of orbital changes, and its drying had lasting consequences.", "Scientists have finally settled the debate about how quickly the Sahara dried out."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. ציורי הסלע הם ראיה אחת מהפסקה השלישית, לא הרעיון המרכזי.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה מהפסקה השנייה, אבל היא רק ההסבר לגורם ולא הקטע כולו, שעוסק גם בראיות ובתוצאות.", "נכון. הקטע מתאר את התקופה הלחה, את הסיבה המסלולית שלה, את הראיות לקיומה ואת ההשלכות של סיומה על אוכלוסיות האזור.", "לא נכון. הפסקה הרביעית מציינת במפורש שאופן סיום התקופה עדיין שנוי במחלוקת."]$q$::jsonb, $q$main_idea$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=green-sahara, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the third paragraph, all of the following are true EXCEPT —$q$, $q$["Atlantic sediment cores show that dust from Africa increased during the humid period.", "Rock art in North African mountains depicts animals that could not live there now.", "A cave in the Egyptian desert contains images of figures that seem to be swimming.", "The evidence for a greener Sahara is plentiful."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. זו הקביעה השגויה — הפסקה כותבת שגלעיני המשקע מראים ירידה חדה בכמות האבק בתקופה הלחה, לא עלייה.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השלישית, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — ציורי הסלע מתארים בקר, ג'ירפות והיפופוטמים.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השלישית, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — המערה במדבר המצרי מכילה דמויות שנראות שוחות.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השלישית, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — הפסקה פותחת בכך שהראיות רבות ומרשימות."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=green-sahara, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the second paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["describe the rock paintings that record the animals of the green Sahara.", "present the disagreement over how quickly the humid period ended.", "explain how migrating herders contributed to the rise of ancient Egypt.", "explain the astronomical and environmental mechanisms that produced the Sahara's long humid period."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. ציורי הסלע מתוארים בפסקה השלישית.", "לא נכון. המחלוקת על קצב ההתייבשות מוצגת בפסקה הרביעית.", "לא נכון. ההגירה לעמק הנילוס מוזכרת בסוף הפסקה הרביעית.", "נכון. הפסקה השנייה מסבירה כיצד תנודת ציר כדור הארץ חיזקה את המונסון וכיצד הצמחייה הגבירה את ההשפעה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=green-sahara, q3$q$, 3, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$It can be inferred from the fourth paragraph that —$q$, $q$["the population of the Nile valley declined sharply as the Sahara dried.", "the drying of the Sahara may have indirectly influenced the development of Egyptian civilization.", "researchers now agree that the monsoon collapsed within a few centuries.", "the pastoral communities of the interior remained in place despite the drought."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה מתארת דווקא ריכוז אוכלוסייה בעמק הנילוס, לא ירידה.", "נכון. הפסקה כותבת שהרועים נדדו לעמק הנילוס ושחוקרים מסוימים סבורים כי הגעתם תרמה לריכוז האוכלוסייה שקדם לעליית מצרים העתיקה.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מציגה מחלוקת — חוקרים אחרים טוענים שההתייבשות הייתה הדרגתית.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מציינת במפורש שהקהילות נטשו את פנים היבשת."]$q$::jsonb, $q$inference$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=green-sahara, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$In the fourth paragraph, the word "contend" is closest in meaning to —$q$, $q$["Compete with one another for resources", "Deny without offering any evidence", "Measure with scientific instruments", "Argue"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. זו משמעות אחרת של המילה (להתחרות), שאינה מתאימה לוויכוח מדעי.", "לא נכון. החוקרים מציגים עמדה, לא מכחישים ללא ראיות.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה עוסקת במדידה.", "נכון. 'contend' פירושו טוענים, מציגים עמדה בוויכוח — חוקרים אחרים טוענים שההתייבשות הייתה הדרגתית."]$q$::jsonb, $q$vocab_in_context$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["Others contend that the drying was gradual"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=green-sahara, q5$q$, 5, true);
  end if;

  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$Urban Heat Islands$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$Urban Heat Islands$q$, $q$In the early nineteenth century, an amateur meteorologist named Luke Howard noticed that London was consistently warmer than the surrounding countryside. His careful measurements, published over several years, provided the first systematic description of what is now called the urban heat island. The term describes a simple but important pattern: cities are warmer than the rural areas around them, and the difference is greatest at night. In large cities the gap can reach several degrees, with significant effects on energy use and human health.

Several factors combine to produce the effect. Asphalt, concrete, and dark roofs absorb sunlight during the day and release the stored heat slowly after sunset. Tall buildings trap this warmth between them and block the wind that might otherwise carry it away. Cities also contain far less vegetation than the countryside, so they lose the cooling that occurs when plants release water vapor. Finally, vehicles, factories, and air conditioners generate waste heat of their own, adding to the burden.

The consequences are far from trivial. Higher temperatures increase the demand for cooling, which raises electricity consumption and, in turn, pollution from power plants. During heat waves, the extra warmth can be dangerous, particularly for elderly residents and people without air conditioning. Nevertheless, cities are not powerless. Planting trees, installing green roofs, and painting surfaces in light colors that reflect sunlight have all been shown to lower local temperatures. Some cities have even coated streets with reflective materials, although the long-term benefits of such measures are still being assessed.$q$, $q$environment / geography$q$, 5, 252, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_D$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the first paragraph, what did Luke Howard discover?$q$, $q$["London's temperature was rising steadily from year to year.", "The countryside around London was warmer than the city itself.", "London was regularly warmer than the rural areas nearby.", "London's temperature varied more at night than during the day."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה מדברת על הבדל בין העיר לסביבתה, לא על עלייה משנה לשנה.", "לא נכון. זה ההפך ממה שנאמר — העיר הייתה חמה יותר מהכפר.", "נכון. הפסקה הראשונה כותבת שהווארד הבחין שלונדון חמה בעקביות מהאזור הכפרי שסביבה.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מציינת שההפרש בין עיר לכפר גדול ביותר בלילה, לא שהטמפרטורה של לונדון משתנה יותר בלילה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch D, passage=heat-islands, q1$q$, 1, true);
