  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$The Erie Canal$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$The Erie Canal$q$, $q$When the Erie Canal was proposed in the early nineteenth century, many Americans considered the plan absurd. The waterway would have to stretch more than 360 miles across New York State, from the Hudson River to Lake Erie, through forests, swamps and rocky ridges. The federal government refused to fund it, and critics mocked the project as "Clinton's Ditch," after Governor DeWitt Clinton, its most determined champion. The state legislature nevertheless approved the money in 1817, and digging began that summer near the town of Rome.

The builders faced a serious problem: the United States had almost no trained civil engineers at the time. The men who directed the work were largely surveyors and lawyers who learned their craft as the canal advanced. They devised new tools for pulling stumps and clearing land, and they invented a cement that hardened underwater. Dozens of locks were needed to lift boats over the changes in elevation between the river and the lake. Because so many engineers gained their training on the project, the canal has been called the country's first school of engineering.

The canal opened in October 1825, and its effects were felt almost immediately. Freight that had once been hauled overland at enormous cost could now travel by water for a small fraction of the price. Grain and timber flowed east from the interior, while manufactured goods and settlers moved west along the same route. New York City, at the mouth of the Hudson, quickly became the nation's leading port. Towns along the canal, such as Rochester and Buffalo, grew from tiny settlements into thriving cities. Within about a decade, tolls had repaid the entire cost of construction, silencing the critics who had once laughed at the ditch.$q$, $q$history / economics$q$, 4, 285, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_G$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$Which of the following is NOT mentioned in the first paragraph?$q$, $q$["The federal government declined to pay for the project.", "Critics gave the canal a mocking nickname.", "The canal had to cross forests, swamps and rocky ridges.", "Governor Clinton personally invested much of his own fortune in the digging."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה הראשונה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — הממשל הפדרלי סירב לממן את הפרויקט.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה הראשונה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — המבקרים כינו את התעלה 'התעלה של קלינטון' בלעג.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה הראשונה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — התעלה נחפרה דרך יערות, ביצות ורכסי סלע.", "נכון. זו הקביעה שאינה מופיעה — הפסקה מתארת את קלינטון כתומך הנחוש של הפרויקט, אך אינה אומרת שהשקיע בו את הונו הפרטי."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch G, passage=erie, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the passage, why has the canal been called "the country's first school of engineering"?$q$, $q$["Because many of the men who built it acquired their engineering skills on the job.", "Because the state of New York opened a special college for engineers beside the canal in 1817.", "Because its designers had been trained at the leading engineering schools of Europe.", "Because engineering students were required to study its locks before graduating."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. הפסקה השנייה אומרת שהמנהלים היו מודדים ועורכי דין שלמדו את המקצוע תוך כדי העבודה, ולכן התעלה נחשבת לבית הספר הראשון להנדסה.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר פתיחת מכללה.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אומרת ההפך — כמעט לא היו בארצות הברית מהנדסים מוכשרים.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר דרישה כזו מסטודנטים."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["the canal has been called the country's first school of engineering"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch G, passage=erie, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the third paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["explain how the builders overcame their lack of formal training.", "describe the economic transformation the canal produced once it opened.", "describe the political battle over funding the canal in 1817.", "list the new tools and materials the builders invented during the construction."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. התמודדות הבונים עם חוסר ההכשרה היא נושא הפסקה השנייה.", "נכון. הפסקה מתארת את ירידת עלויות ההובלה, זרימת הסחורות, עליית ניו יורק כנמל וצמיחת הערים.", "לא נכון. המאבק על המימון מתואר בפסקה הראשונה.", "לא נכון. הכלים והמלט החדשים נזכרים בפסקה השנייה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch G, passage=erie, q3$q$, 3, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$Based on the passage as a whole, what can be inferred about the canal's early critics?$q$, $q$["They were mostly engineers who understood the technical problems better than Clinton.", "They succeeded in delaying the start of construction for several years.", "Their doubts were proved wrong by the canal's rapid commercial success.", "They continued to oppose the canal even after it had repaid its cost."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. הקטע אומר שכמעט לא היו מהנדסים מוכשרים במדינה, ואינו מזהה את המבקרים כמהנדסים.", "לא נכון. הפסקה הראשונה אומרת שהחפירה החלה בקיץ 1817, מיד לאחר האישור.", "נכון. הפסקה האחרונה אומרת שהאגרות החזירו את עלות הבנייה בתוך כעשור והשתיקו את המבקרים — כלומר ספקותיהם התבדו.", "לא נכון. הקטע אומר שההצלחה 'השתיקה' את המבקרים, לא שהמשיכו להתנגד."]$q$::jsonb, $q$inference$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch G, passage=erie, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$In the third paragraph, the word "thriving" is closest in meaning to —$q$, $q$["crowded and dangerous", "carefully planned by engineers", "located along a waterway", "prosperous"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. המילה מתארת הצלחה, לא סכנה.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה קשורה לתכנון.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה מתארת מיקום.", "נכון. 'thriving' פירושו משגשג — הערים לאורך התעלה צמחו מיישובים זעירים לערים פורחות."]$q$::jsonb, $q$vocab_in_context$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["thriving cities"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch G, passage=erie, q5$q$, 5, true);
