      values (v_pid, $q$In the sentence "Because the flaw was uniform across the entire surface, it could, in principle, be corrected," the word "it" refers to —$q$, $q$["the surface", "the telescope", "the flaw", "the principle"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. המשפט אומר שמשהו ניתן לתיקון, והדבר שמתקנים הוא הפגם, לא פני השטח.", "לא נכון. הטלסקופ אינו מוזכר במשפט, ו-'it' מתייחס לנושא המשפט — הפגם.", "נכון. 'it' מתייחס ל-'the flaw' — הפגם היה אחיד, ולכן ניתן היה לתקן אותו.", "לא נכון. 'in principle' הוא ביטוי שפירושו 'באופן עקרוני', ואינו נושא המשפט."]$q$::jsonb, $q$reference_word$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["Because the flaw was uniform across the entire surface, it could, in principle, be corrected"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=hubble-mirror, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$Based on the statement that the mirror "had been polished precisely to the wrong specification," what can be inferred about the manufacturing process?$q$, $q$["The workers who polished the mirror lacked the skill to meet the required standard.", "The specification was changed several times while the mirror was being made.", "The polishing was rushed in order to meet the deadline for the launch.", "The work itself was highly accurate but was guided by a faulty target."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. המשפט מדגיש שהליטוש נעשה בדיוק רב, כלומר המיומנות לא הייתה הבעיה.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר שינויים במפרט.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר לחץ זמן.", "נכון. המשפט אומר שהמראה לוטשה במדויק, אך למפרט שגוי — כלומר הביצוע היה מדויק והכיוון היה מוטעה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$inference$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["it had been polished precisely to the wrong specification"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=hubble-mirror, q5$q$, 5, true);
  end if;

  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$Fermat's Last Theorem and Andrew Wiles$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$Fermat's Last Theorem and Andrew Wiles$q$, $q$Around 1637, the French mathematician Pierre de Fermat wrote a brief note in the margin of a book he was reading. He claimed to have found a remarkable proof that a certain equation had no whole-number solutions when the exponent was greater than two. The margin, he added, was too narrow to contain it. Fermat never published the proof, and after his death the claim became known as Fermat's Last Theorem.

The statement itself is simple enough for a schoolchild to understand, yet it resisted every attempt at proof for more than three centuries. Leading mathematicians settled particular cases, and prizes were offered for a general solution. Thousands of flawed proofs were submitted by amateurs and professionals alike. By the twentieth century, many experts doubted whether Fermat had really possessed a valid argument at all, and the problem had come to symbolize the limits of mathematical knowledge.

Andrew Wiles first encountered the theorem as a ten-year-old in a public library in Cambridge and resolved to solve it. Decades later, as a professor at Princeton, he worked on the problem in near secrecy for seven years. Rather than attacking the equation directly, he built on modern theories connecting elliptic curves and modular forms, fields that Fermat could never have imagined. In 1993, he announced his proof at a conference in Cambridge, to worldwide attention.

The story did not end there, however. Reviewers found a gap in one part of the argument, and for over a year Wiles struggled to close it. Working with his former student Richard Taylor, he finally repaired the proof in 1994, and it was published the following year. The achievement showed that a problem posed in a margin could drive the development of entire branches of mathematics.$q$, $q$mathematics$q$, 6, 287, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_I$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$What is the main idea of the passage?$q$, $q$["A claim scribbled in a margin defied mathematicians for more than three centuries until Wiles finally proved it using modern methods.", "Pierre de Fermat deliberately hid his proof because he wanted to challenge future generations of mathematicians.", "Andrew Wiles decided as a child to solve the theorem after reading about it in a library in Cambridge.", "Thousands of incorrect proofs were submitted over the years by both amateur and professional mathematicians."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. הקטע עוקב אחרי הטענה מהערת השוליים של פרמה, דרך מאות שנות כישלון, ועד להוכחה של ויילס בכלים מודרניים.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו טוען שפרמה הסתיר את ההוכחה בכוונה; הוא רק ציין שהשוליים צרים מדי.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה מהפסקה השלישית, אך היא פרט ביוגרפי ולא הרעיון המרכזי.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה מהפסקה השנייה, אך היא פרט אחד בלבד בתולדות הבעיה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$main_idea$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=fermat, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the second paragraph, all of the following are true EXCEPT —$q$, $q$["The theorem can be understood even by someone with a basic education.", "A complete proof for all cases was found shortly after Fermat's death.", "Rewards were offered to anyone who could produce a general proof.", "Some experts came to doubt that Fermat ever had a correct proof."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השנייה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — הטענה פשוטה דיה כדי שילד בבית ספר יבין אותה.", "נכון. זו הקביעה השגויה — הפסקה כותבת שהבעיה עמדה בפני כל ניסיון הוכחה במשך יותר משלוש מאות שנה, ורק מקרים פרטיים נפתרו.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השנייה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — הוצעו פרסים על פתרון כללי.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה על פי הפסקה השנייה, ולכן אינה החריג המבוקש — במאה העשרים מומחים רבים פקפקו בכך שלפרמה הייתה הוכחה תקפה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, $q$["it resisted every attempt at proof for more than three centuries"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=fermat, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the fourth paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["explain the modern mathematical theories on which Wiles based his proof.", "describe the note that Fermat wrote in the margin of his book.", "show that the proof had a serious flaw that took considerable effort to repair.", "list the many mathematicians who attempted to prove the theorem over the centuries."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. התיאוריות המודרניות מוזכרות בפסקה השלישית, לא ברביעית.", "לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה הראשונה — ההערה בשוליים — ולא הפסקה הרביעית.", "נכון. הפסקה מתארת את הפער שנמצא בהוכחה, את המאבק של ויילס במשך יותר משנה ואת התיקון בעזרת טיילור.", "לא נכון. הניסיונות הרבים מוזכרים בפסקה השנייה, לא ברביעית."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=fermat, q3$q$, 3, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$In the second paragraph, the word "resisted" is closest in meaning to —$q$, $q$["encouraged and rewarded people who made an effort", "was rejected by the mathematical community as unimportant", "was gradually forgotten by nearly everyone", "held out against"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. המילה מתארת עמידה בפני ניסיונות, לא עידוד שלהם.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה עוסקת בדחייה על ידי הקהילה; הבעיה דווקא משכה תשומת לב רבה.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה עוסקת בשכחה; הבעיה נותרה מפורסמת.", "נכון. 'resisted' פירושו עמדה בפני, החזיקה מעמד מול — הבעיה לא נכנעה לשום ניסיון הוכחה במשך מאות שנים."]$q$::jsonb, $q$vocab_in_context$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["it resisted every attempt at proof for more than three centuries"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=fermat, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the passage, what did Wiles do "rather than attacking the equation directly"?$q$, $q$["He drew on recent mathematical theories that Fermat could not have known.", "He searched old libraries for the original proof that Fermat had described.", "He collected and analyzed the thousands of flawed proofs submitted earlier.", "He announced the result publicly before he had completed the argument."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. הפסקה השלישית כותבת שוויילס התבסס על תיאוריות מודרניות של עקומים אליפטיים ותבניות מודולריות, תחומים שפרמה לא יכול היה לדמיין.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר חיפוש אחר ההוכחה המקורית של פרמה.", "לא נכון. ההוכחות השגויות מוזכרות בפסקה השנייה, ולא כחלק משיטת העבודה של ויילס.", "לא נכון. ויילס הכריז על ההוכחה ב-1993 לאחר שבע שנות עבודה, והפער נתגלה רק בבדיקה שלאחר מכן."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["Rather than attacking the equation directly, he built on modern theories connecting elliptic curves and modular forms"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=fermat, q5$q$, 5, true);
  end if;
end $$;
do $$ declare v_pid uuid; begin

  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$Redefining the Kilogram$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$Redefining the Kilogram$q$, $q$For more than a century, the kilogram was defined by a physical object. A cylinder of platinum and iridium, made in 1889 and kept in a vault near Paris, served as the international prototype. Every scale in the world was ultimately calibrated against this single piece of metal. The arrangement worked, yet it had an obvious weakness. If the cylinder gained or lost mass, the definition of the kilogram changed with it, and there was no external standard against which to check.

Over the decades, comparisons with official copies suggested that the prototype's mass had indeed drifted by tens of micrograms. Scientists could not even say whether the original had lost mass or the copies had gained it. Since all the other base units of measurement had already been tied to constants of nature, the kilogram became an increasingly awkward exception. Metrologists therefore sought a definition based on a fixed value of the Planck constant, a fundamental quantity of quantum physics.

Achieving this required instruments capable of measuring mass in terms of electrical and quantum quantities with extraordinary precision. After years of refinement, laboratories in several countries produced results that agreed closely enough to proceed. In November 2018, representatives of over sixty nations voted to adopt the new definition, which took effect the following May. For ordinary users, nothing changed; a kilogram of flour still weighs a kilogram. However, the unit is now anchored to a constant that is the same everywhere in the universe, rather than to a lump of metal in a French vault.$q$, $q$science / physics$q$, 6, 254, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_I$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$What is the main idea of the passage?$q$, $q$["A metal cylinder kept near Paris served as the world's standard of mass for over a hundred years.", "The kilogram was moved from a definition based on a physical object to one based on a constant of nature.", "Scientists discovered that the international prototype had lost tens of micrograms of mass over time.", "Everyday weights and measures were left completely unchanged by the decision taken in 2018."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה מהפסקה הראשונה, אך היא מתארת רק את המצב הישן ולא את השינוי שהקטע עוסק בו.", "נכון. הקטע מתאר את ההגדרה הישנה, את חולשתה, ואת המעבר להגדרה המבוססת על קבוע פלאנק — זהו הרעיון המרכזי.", "לא נכון. הפסקה השנייה מציינת שאי אפשר היה לדעת אם המקור איבד מסה או שההעתקים צברו, ובכל מקרה זה פרט בלבד.", "לא נכון. זו קביעה נכונה מהפסקה השלישית, אך היא רק הערת סיום ולא הרעיון המרכזי."]$q$::jsonb, $q$main_idea$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=kilogram, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the second paragraph, what made the kilogram different from the other base units of measurement?$q$, $q$["It was the only unit that had been defined more than a century earlier.", "It was the only unit that scientists in different countries could not agree on.", "It alone was still defined by an object rather than by a constant of nature.", "It was the only unit whose value could be measured with quantum instruments."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה אינה משווה את גיל ההגדרות של היחידות.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אינה מזכירה חילוקי דעות בין מדינות.", "נכון. הפסקה כותבת שכל שאר יחידות הבסיס כבר נקשרו לקבועי טבע, ולכן הקילוגרם נותר יוצא דופן מביך.", "לא נכון. המדידה בכלים קוונטיים מוזכרת כפתרון בפסקה השלישית, לא כמה שהבדיל את הקילוגרם."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, $q$["Since all the other base units of measurement had already been tied to constants of nature, the kilogram became an increasingly awkward exception"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=kilogram, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the first paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["explain how the Planck constant can be used to define a unit of mass.", "describe the international vote that approved the new definition in 2018.", "report that the mass of the prototype had drifted by tens of micrograms.", "present the old definition of the kilogram and the weakness that was built into it."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. קבוע פלאנק מוזכר רק בסוף הפסקה השנייה.", "לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה השלישית — ההצבעה ב-2018 — ולא הפסקה הראשונה.", "לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה השנייה — הסחיפה במסה — ולא הפסקה הראשונה.", "נכון. הפסקה מציגה את הגליל מפלטינה ואירידיום כהגדרת הקילוגרם ואת החולשה שבהסתמכות על עצם יחיד."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=kilogram, q3$q$, 3, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$In the first paragraph, the word "calibrated" most nearly means —$q$, $q$["adjusted to a standard", "weighed on a very sensitive scale", "protected carefully against any damage", "sold in a busy market"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. 'calibrated' פירושו כוונן או הותאם לפי תקן — כל המאזניים בעולם כוונו לפי גליל המתכת.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה מתארת פעולת שקילה, אלא התאמה לתקן.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה עוסקת בהגנה.", "לא נכון. המילה אינה קשורה למכירה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$vocab_in_context$q$, $q$anchor$q$, $q$["Every scale in the world was ultimately calibrated against this single piece of metal"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=kilogram, q4$q$, 4, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$Based on the passage, what can be inferred about the practical effect of the 2018 redefinition?$q$, $q$["Scales around the world had to be replaced with new quantum instruments.", "The basis of the unit changed while everyday measurements stayed the same.", "A kilogram now weighs slightly less than it did before the redefinition.", "The old platinum cylinder was destroyed once the new definition took effect."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה השלישית כותבת שעבור משתמשים רגילים דבר לא השתנה.", "נכון. הפסקה השלישית קובעת שקילוגרם קמח עדיין שוקל קילוגרם, אך היחידה מעוגנת כעת בקבוע טבע ולא בגוש מתכת.", "לא נכון. הקטע כותב במפורש שדבר לא השתנה במדידות היומיומיות.", "לא נכון. הקטע אינו מזכיר את גורל הגליל הישן."]$q$::jsonb, $q$inference$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=kilogram, q5$q$, 5, true);
  end if;

  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$The Apollo Guidance Computer$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$The Apollo Guidance Computer$q$, $q$When President Kennedy committed the United States to landing on the moon before 1970, no computer existed that could guide a spacecraft there. Ground stations could track a vehicle and send instructions, but radio signals took over a second to reach the moon. During critical moments, such as the final descent, the astronauts needed a machine on board that could make calculations instantly. The task of building it fell to the Instrumentation Laboratory at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

The result was the Apollo Guidance Computer, a box weighing about thirty kilograms that fit into a space the size of a small suitcase. By modern standards its power was tiny; a basic mobile phone today has far more memory and speed. Nevertheless, it was among the first computers to rely on integrated circuits, at a time when most machines still used bulky transistors. Its programs were stored in a form of memory made by threading fine wires through tiny magnetic rings, a process so delicate that it was largely done by hand.

The software was as innovative as the hardware. Led by Margaret Hamilton, the programming team designed the system so that it could rank tasks by importance and drop less urgent ones when overloaded. This feature proved decisive during the landing of Apollo 11 in July 1969. Minutes before touchdown, alarms warned that the computer was receiving more data than it could handle. Instead of failing, it discarded low-priority work and kept the essential guidance calculations running.

Because the computer stayed on task, mission controllers gave the crew permission to continue, and Neil Armstrong landed safely. The Apollo Guidance Computer never received the fame of the rockets or the astronauts. Yet many historians regard it as a turning point in computing, since it proved that small, reliable machines could be trusted with human lives.$q$, $q$technology / history$q$, 5, 302, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_I$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$An appropriate title for this text would be —$q$, $q$["Margaret Hamilton and the Birth of Software Engineering", "Why Radio Signals Are Too Slow for Space Travel", "The Small Machine That Guided Astronauts to the Moon", "How Modern Phones Surpassed the Computers of the 1960s"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. המילטון מוזכרת בפסקה השלישית בלבד, והקטע עוסק במחשב כולו, לא רק בתוכנה.", "לא נכון. השהיית האותות היא רק ההסבר לצורך במחשב, בפסקה הראשונה.", "נכון. הקטע כולו מתאר את מחשב הניווט של אפולו — הצורך בו, החומרה, התוכנה ותפקידו בנחיתה.", "לא נכון. ההשוואה לטלפונים מודרניים היא הערת אגב אחת בפסקה השנייה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$main_idea$q$, $q$text$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=apollo-computer, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the first paragraph, why was a computer on board the spacecraft necessary?$q$, $q$["Ground stations were unable to track the spacecraft once it left Earth's orbit.", "The astronauts had not been trained to perform navigation calculations themselves.", "President Kennedy had specifically demanded that a computer be included.", "Instructions from Earth arrived too slowly for moments that demanded immediate decisions."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$["לא נכון. הפסקה כותבת שתחנות הקרקע יכלו לעקוב אחרי החללית ולשלוח הוראות.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אינה מזכירה את הכשרת האסטרונאוטים.", "לא נכון. קנדי התחייב לנחיתה על הירח; הפסקה אינה מייחסת לו דרישה לגבי מחשב.", "נכון. הפסקה מסבירה שאותות רדיו נדרשו ליותר משנייה כדי להגיע לירח, ולכן ברגעים קריטיים כמו הנחיתה נדרש מחשב שמחשב מיידית."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, $q$["radio signals took over a second to reach the moon"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=apollo-computer, q2$q$, 2, true);
