  if not exists (select 1 from reading_passages where title = $q$The Invention of Zero$q$) then
    insert into reading_passages(title, body, topic, difficulty, word_count, is_published, generation_batch)
      values ($q$The Invention of Zero$q$, $q$It is easy to assume that zero has always been part of arithmetic, but the idea developed slowly and in stages. Early civilizations counted objects, and nobody needed a symbol for the absence of objects. The Babylonians, writing around 300 BCE, used a placeholder mark to show an empty position within a number, much as the zero in 205 separates the two from the five. However, this mark was never used on its own and had no meaning as a quantity. The Greeks and Romans, for their part, managed without any such symbol at all.

The decisive step was taken in India. By the seventh century, Indian mathematicians treated zero as a number in its own right, one that could be added, subtracted, and multiplied like any other. The scholar Brahmagupta, writing in 628, set out rules for calculating with zero and even attempted to define division by it. Zero thus acquired both a symbol and a role. This new understanding, combined with the place-value system, made written arithmetic far simpler than the Roman numerals still used in Europe.

The concept spread westward through the Islamic world, where scholars in Baghdad translated Indian works and refined the methods. In the early thirteenth century, the Italian mathematician Fibonacci, who had learned the system as a boy in North Africa, introduced it to European merchants. Some authorities distrusted the new numerals, and a few cities even banned them for a time. Nevertheless, their convenience eventually won out, and zero became the quiet foundation of modern science and commerce.$q$, $q$mathematics / history$q$, 5, 253, true, $q$reading_shabbat_2026-09-05_I$q$)
      returning id into v_pid;
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$According to the first paragraph, how did the Babylonian mark differ from a true zero?$q$, $q$["It showed an empty position but did not represent a quantity by itself.", "It was used only by priests and was unknown to ordinary merchants.", "It appeared only at the end of a number and never in the middle.", "It was borrowed from the Greeks, who had invented it earlier."]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$["נכון. הפסקה כותבת שהסימן ציין מקום ריק בתוך מספר, אך מעולם לא שימש לבדו ולא היה לו משמעות של כמות.", "לא נכון. הפסקה אינה מזכירה כוהנים או סוחרים.", "לא נכון. הדוגמה בפסקה (205) מראה סימן באמצע המספר.", "לא נכון. הפסקה כותבת שהיוונים והרומאים הסתדרו ללא סימן כזה כלל."]$q$::jsonb, $q$explicit_detail$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, $q$["this mark was never used on its own and had no meaning as a quantity"]$q$::jsonb, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=zero, q1$q$, 1, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the second paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["explain why the Greeks and Romans never developed a symbol for zero.", "describe the breakthrough in India that turned zero into a genuine number.", "trace the path by which the new numerals reached European merchants.", "compare the Babylonian placeholder with the Roman system of numerals."]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$["לא נכון. היוונים והרומאים מוזכרים בפסקה הראשונה, והקטע אינו מסביר מדוע לא פיתחו סמל.", "נכון. הפסקה מתארת כיצד מתמטיקאים הודים, ובראשם ברהמגופטה, התייחסו לאפס כמספר לכל דבר וקבעו כללים לחישוב איתו.", "לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה השלישית — הדרך לאירופה — ולא הפסקה השנייה.", "לא נכון. ההשוואה הזו אינה מופיעה; הספרות הרומיות מוזכרות רק בקצרה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=zero, q2$q$, 2, true);
    insert into reading_questions(passage_id, question_text, options, correct_option_index, explanations_he, question_type, window_size, highlight_spans, qa_note, display_order, is_published)
      values (v_pid, $q$The main purpose of the last paragraph is to —$q$, $q$["present the rules that Brahmagupta set out for calculating with zero.", "explain why early civilizations had no need for a symbol for nothing.", "trace how zero traveled to Europe and was eventually accepted there.", "argue that Fibonacci was the true inventor of the modern number system."]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$["לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה השנייה — כללי ברהמגופטה — ולא הפסקה האחרונה.", "לא נכון. זהו תוכן הפסקה הראשונה — היעדר הצורך בסמל — ולא הפסקה האחרונה.", "נכון. הפסקה עוקבת אחרי מסע הרעיון מבגדאד דרך פיבונאצ'י אל סוחרי אירופה, דרך ההתנגדות ועד לקבלתו.", "לא נכון. הפסקה מציגה את פיבונאצ'י כמי שהביא את השיטה לאירופה, לא כממציאה."]$q$::jsonb, $q$paragraph_purpose$q$, $q$paragraph$q$, null, $q$shabbat batch I, passage=zero, q3$q$, 3, true);
